<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The protocol core as a single assembly.

  Both the app and the background agent need it, and the app references the
  agent so its DLL ships in the package. Compiling the sources into each project
  separately gave every type two identities - the compiler warned about roughly
  thirty of them, and a TextMessage from the agent would not have been
  assignable to a TextMessage in the app. One assembly, referenced twice, is
  the fix.

  The desktop harness still links the same sources rather than referencing this
  project: it targets .NET 4.5, which cannot reference a Windows Phone library.
  That is harmless - it is a separate build with no shared binary.
-->
